  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 9 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: 11 tests in total, 0 failed.\n\n- **Diacritics:** `đ` and `Đ` are mapped to `d` first. The text is then decomposed and the combining marks are stripped, so Vietnamese and other Latin accents become plain ASCII.\n- **Separators:** the text is lowercased, and every run of characters outside a-z and 0-9 becomes one hyphen. Leading and trailing hyphens are removed.\n- **Length:** the slug is cut at 50 characters, and any hyphen left at the end of the cut is removed. For example, 49 `a`s followed by a space and `bbb` gives 49 `a`s.\n\nThe tests cover plain lowercasing, Vietnamese and other Latin accents, symbol runs, trimming, input with only symbols (returns an empty string), and the truncation cases.\n\nThe tool reported that `test/strings.test.js` changed on disk after I edited it. The contents match what I wrote, so I left it as is.",
